WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.601
Joining us now to discuss is Republican

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.004
Senator Bill Cassidy of Louisiana.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.105
Senator, thanks for joining us.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.473
So a potential default could

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.141
now just now just be 11 days

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.075
away, theoretically.

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:10.477
President Biden said today

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.578
that he's done his part.

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.847
Now it's time for Republicans to move.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:15.815
How worried are you that

00:00:15.815 --> 00:00:17.283
a catastrophic default

00:00:17.283 --> 00:00:18.752
could actually happen

00:00:18.752 --> 00:00:20.687
and do you think Republicans

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:21.855
who are negotiating

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:25.692
need to be willing to move more

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.293
Well, a couple of things.

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.261
First,
I think the president

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.562
needs to show leadership.

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:31.531
He took about 100 days to gauge,

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:32.799
you know, to kick in.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:34.334
And now that he's finally negotiating,

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.336
I'm pleased that he's doing so.

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.071
But I also want to point out

00:00:38.071 --> 00:00:40.306
that Secretary Yellen's comment

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.175
about one default occurs

00:00:42.175 --> 00:00:44.077
potentially as very early

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:45.445
as the 1st of June.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.013
But it could be later.

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.449
Well, let's have a little leadership.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:51.251
The financial markets are all nervous

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:51.851
about this.

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.220
Is it the first or is that the 14th?

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.021
A quarterly

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.189
payment of taxes

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.490
comes to the federal government

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.125
beginning on the 15th,

00:00:59.125 --> 00:00:59.893
at which point

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.995
the risk of default is averted.

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:04.130
So the president just needs to step up

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.565
and calm down the markets

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.933
by being specific.

00:01:06.933 --> 00:01:07.934
And lastly,

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:08.568
the president

00:01:08.568 --> 00:01:09.702
has been jacking up

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:11.171
spending in his first two years

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.472
of the presidency.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:13.740
Now he wants Republicans

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.675
to accept that as a new baseline.

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:16.709
I think Republicans

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:18.578
and the American people

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.346
are reasonable to say, Mr.

00:01:20.346 --> 00:01:20.814
President,

00:01:20.814 --> 00:01:21.581
just because

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.416
you have artificially inflated

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.051
spending for the first two years

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.252
of your presidency,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:26.853
by the way,

00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:28.288
given us all kinds of inflation

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:29.289
to boot it,

00:01:29.289 --> 00:01:30.990
does that become the new baseline?

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.059
We don't think it necessarily has to.

00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:34.694
And I think Republicans are reasonable

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.030
to ask that it be reset back down.

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:37.464
Yeah,

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:38.765
you're referring to the fact

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:39.199
that the White

00:01:39.199 --> 00:01:40.567
House, according to reports,

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:42.368
offered to

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:42.802
as part of

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:43.503
this negotiation,

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:44.571
offered to freeze spending,

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:45.805
I think at 20,

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:48.975
22 levels, whereas obviously McCarthy

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:49.742
and the Republicans

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.610
negotiating wanted

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.878
wanted it to be frozen

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.680
at an earlier levels.

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:54.547
The House Freedom

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:55.448
Caucus is

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.916
a group of very conservative

00:01:56.916 --> 00:01:57.750
Republicans in the House

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.252
Republican Caucus.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.120
They're saying that

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.287
they're going to oppose basically

00:02:01.287 --> 00:02:02.422
any compromises

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.557
to the original legislation.

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.325
That they passed

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:08.261
a majority of the House Republican Party.

00:02:08.261 --> 00:02:11.431
We should note, voted to not count

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:12.165
electoral votes

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:13.600
from Arizona and Pennsylvania.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:14.934
Based on election lies,

00:02:14.934 --> 00:02:16.803
the lies that you stood up against.

00:02:16.803 --> 00:02:18.338
Do you think the House Republican caucus

00:02:18.338 --> 00:02:19.105
can be counted on

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.707
to arrive at a reasonable compromise

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.142
in these debt negotiations,

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:25.578
given that fact, that ugly fact that

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.780
that sometimes they

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.883
take pretty extreme positions

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:34.621
Well, I think that the tea

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.622
I have strong feelings

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:37.557
about about the last election

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:38.825
and how that transpired.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:39.459
But nonetheless,

00:02:39.459 --> 00:02:41.561
I think that's a totally separate issue.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.530
And let's give a tip of the hat

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:45.365
to Kevin McCarthy,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.499
the package

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.334
that he sent to the president.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.602
He had Republicans

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:51.905
voting for a debt ceiling increase

00:02:52.138 --> 00:02:54.240
who had never previously voted for a debt

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:55.475
ceiling increase.

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.576
And I don't think we're going to allow

00:02:56.576 --> 00:02:58.278
anxiety, existential anxiety

00:02:58.278 --> 00:02:59.345
about the future

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.481
to kind of dictate what is done today.

00:03:01.481 --> 00:03:03.750
Once Kevin said in a private meeting,

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.351
never asked me to do something

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:06.920
because you think I can't.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.021
Let me first go out there

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:09.489
and see if I can.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:10.490
I think the president needs

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:11.691
to step forward

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.359
make an earnest effort

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:14.627
to meet Republicans

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:16.129
and the American people

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:16.896
on the issue

00:03:16.896 --> 00:03:18.665
of lowering our indebtedness.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:19.499
And if they do so,

00:03:19.499 --> 00:03:21.034
let's see what McCarthy can do.

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.269
And I'd like to have more faith in Kevin.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:24.304
President Biden

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:26.639
also said this morning that he thinks

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:28.107
that he has the authority

00:03:28.107 --> 00:03:29.876
to lift the debt limit on his own

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.078
using the 14th Amendment

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:33.146
though he said it's unclear

00:03:33.146 --> 00:03:34.681
if he has time to use it given the

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:35.782
all the legal challenges

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.783
that would ensue.

00:03:36.783 --> 00:03:37.283
The amendment

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:37.951
says, quote,

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:39.219
The validity of the public debt

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.019
of the United States

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.422
shall not be questioned, unquote,

00:03:42.422 --> 00:03:44.057
I know you don't think he should do this,

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.326
but do you think he's right

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.428
that he has the ability

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:49.796
to use the 14th Amendment

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.130
to raise the debt ceiling on his

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.298
own without Congress

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:56.402
You know, I'm not an attorney.

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.270
It does sound like he's

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.072
kind of squirreling around a little bit.

00:03:59.072 --> 00:04:01.174
His left wing wants him to invoke it.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:04.110
It's one more example of the president's

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.079
taking the constitutionally

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:07.413
delegated authority

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.047
of spending

00:04:08.047 --> 00:04:09.782
from the House of Representatives

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:11.551
and trying to kind of aggregate it

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:12.785
into the White House.

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:14.053
I think the president needs to show

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:14.821
leadership.

00:04:14.821 --> 00:04:15.221
Okay.

00:04:15.221 --> 00:04:16.923
House Republicans, American people,

00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.157
you're concerned about spending.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:19.259
I'll meet you there.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:19.859
As opposed

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:20.827
to finding a dodge

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:21.928
that tries to tries

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:23.363
to work its way around.

00:04:23.363 --> 00:04:24.631
And that's a dodge.

00:04:24.631 --> 00:04:25.531
Meet the mayor of meet

00:04:25.531 --> 00:04:26.266
the American people

00:04:26.266 --> 00:04:27.634
and Republicans where they are.

00:04:27.634 --> 00:04:28.635
I think we can get to where

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:29.435
we need to be.

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.837
I think we can all agree that

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:33.273
that a debt default would be a disaster

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:33.906
or would affect

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:35.008
the economy, would affect

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:36.743
a lot of people out there

00:04:36.743 --> 00:04:38.611
who are watching right now.

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.779
You are part of a group

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.080
of bipartisan senators

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:41.681
who have in

00:04:41.681 --> 00:04:42.482
the past worked out

00:04:42.482 --> 00:04:44.550
other compromises on infrastructure,

00:04:44.884 --> 00:04:47.053
on guns, on other issues.

00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:49.122
Is there a plan B here?

00:04:49.122 --> 00:04:50.723
If we get right up to the moment

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:52.892
that a default could actually happen, is

00:04:52.892 --> 00:04:55.962
is there any sort of, you know, emergency

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.430
legislation to raise the debt

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.631
ceiling for two more months

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.332
or anything like that

00:04:59.332 --> 00:05:01.334
just to make sure that the country

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:03.269
does not plunge into this catastrophe?

00:05:05.838 --> 00:05:07.640
Well, first, I think as I said earlier,

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.410
I think Plan B, my first one is June

00:05:10.543 --> 00:05:11.844
one is the 1st of June

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:13.313
one is the drop dead date

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.847
If it's June 15th,

00:05:14.847 --> 00:05:16.316
is there really an issue

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:18.451
that would calm down financial markets

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:20.219
if the president and Secretary

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:21.754
Yellen came forward with that?

00:05:21.754 --> 00:05:23.222
In terms of the Republican Senate

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.957
coming up with something,

00:05:24.957 --> 00:05:26.459
this is between the president

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:28.328
and the House Republicans.

00:05:28.328 --> 00:05:28.861
And that's

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.196
why it's been so frustrating

00:05:30.196 --> 00:05:32.198
to see the president on the sidelines.

00:05:32.198 --> 00:05:33.733
If the Senate comes up with something,

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:34.901
the House has to accept it

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.202
and the White House does.

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:38.037
So why not just put them together?

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.005
I think Plan B

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:41.107
is to get the president engaged.

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.575
So let's talk about social security,

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:43.910
because if a default happens,

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:45.378
one of the first things to fail

00:05:45.378 --> 00:05:47.046
will be Social Security checks

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:49.015
to seniors who rely upon them.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:50.149
But as you've been sounding

00:05:50.149 --> 00:05:51.684
the alarm about Social Security,

00:05:51.684 --> 00:05:52.352
also faces

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.052
another threat

00:05:53.052 --> 00:05:55.988
in just nine years, estimated insolvency.

00:05:56.622 --> 00:05:58.658
And the top two Republican candidates

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:00.593
for a presidency, Donald Trump

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:01.327
and Ron DeSantis,

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.696
are now
both saying they wouldn't change anything

00:06:03.963 --> 00:06:05.665
about Social Security.

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:06.933
Is that disqualifying?

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:10.837
You know, I think if you

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:11.371
have a leading

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:12.472
presidential candidate,

00:06:12.472 --> 00:06:13.539
be a Joe Biden

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.007
who clearly is saying that.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.142
Are Donald Trump

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.844
pretending to the American people

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:18.211
that there's

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.012
no problem with Social Security

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:21.681
then then they lack the leadership

00:06:21.681 --> 00:06:22.615
to become the president

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:23.950
of the United States?

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:24.450
By the way,

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.952
you can fix Social Security

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.754
and you don't raise taxes on seniors.

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:29.222
You don't cut their benefits.

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.323
And there's a way to do it

00:06:30.323 --> 00:06:32.358
that actually improves the program.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:33.993
But there's no leadership

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.695
like that from Trump or Biden.

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:36.429
In my mind,

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:38.464
that lack of leadership on an issue

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:41.267
so critical to so many Americans

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.403
is disqualifying.

00:06:43.403 --> 00:06:45.171
So you have a plan

00:06:45.171 --> 00:06:47.440
to create a $1.5 trillion fund

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:49.542
that would use investment returns

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:52.412
to fund Social Security.

00:06:52.412 --> 00:06:53.112
Again, we're talking

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:54.013
we're about nine years out

00:06:54.013 --> 00:06:54.781
from insolvency

00:06:54.781 --> 00:06:57.750
estimated given how DC works

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.452
or doesn't work,

00:06:59.452 --> 00:07:00.153
given how we're

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.254
waiting into the last minute

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:01.954
with the debt limit,

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:02.922
we're going to go through this again

00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.057
in the fall with government funding.

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:06.692
Is there

00:07:06.692 --> 00:07:07.593
any willingness

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:09.295
among your colleagues, Democrats

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:10.763
and Republicans in the Senate

00:07:10.763 --> 00:07:12.165
and the House to act

00:07:12.165 --> 00:07:15.301
now to try to fix this problem?

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.870
First, put this in context.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:18.838
US insolvency.

00:07:18.838 --> 00:07:20.873
When insolvency comes in nine years,

00:07:20.873 --> 00:07:22.708
people who are currently receiving

00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:25.545
social benefits will get a 24% cut.

00:07:25.945 --> 00:07:28.014
That's the reason you want to act now.

00:07:28.281 --> 00:07:30.183
And if you wait until the deadline,

00:07:30.183 --> 00:07:31.651
then the cuts are bigger

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.351
and the tax

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:34.620
and or the tax increases are greater.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.988
And so if you want to solve it

00:07:35.988 --> 00:07:37.323
now, without that,

00:07:37.323 --> 00:07:38.791
you need to solve it now.

00:07:38.791 --> 00:07:41.260
And we actually had bipartisan senators

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:43.763
and bipartisan group of representatives

00:07:43.996 --> 00:07:45.264
that were willing to commit

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.499
to this big idea.

00:07:46.499 --> 00:07:49.302
Again, 1.5 trillion in an investment fund

00:07:49.569 --> 00:07:51.604
separate from Social Security.

00:07:51.604 --> 00:07:52.738
And the risk falls

00:07:52.738 --> 00:07:53.573
upon the fund

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:54.774
if the market goes down,

00:07:54.774 --> 00:07:56.576
people still get their benefits.

00:07:56.576 --> 00:07:58.611
No. 24% cut.

00:07:58.611 --> 00:08:00.513
When Joe Biden came out in his State

00:08:00.513 --> 00:08:01.681
of the Union speech

00:08:01.681 --> 00:08:03.583
and began to speak about Republicans

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:05.685
trying to take away your Social Security,

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:07.119
it all fell apart.

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:08.454
The president clearly plans

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:10.590
to run for reelection, as does Joe Biden,

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:12.158
as the Donald Trump

00:08:12.158 --> 00:08:13.459
making Social Security

00:08:13.459 --> 00:08:14.427
an issue

00:08:14.427 --> 00:08:16.562
attacking anyone who comes against them.

00:08:16.562 --> 00:08:18.130
They are ignoring a problem

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:18.698
which is

00:08:18.698 --> 00:08:19.732
which is important

00:08:19.732 --> 00:08:21.300
for seniors, important

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.768
for our nation's indebtedness.

00:08:22.768 --> 00:08:23.269
I wish

00:08:23.269 --> 00:08:25.471
both of them would show real leadership.

00:08:25.471 --> 00:08:26.506
Let me ask you before you go.

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:28.774
Florida Governor Ron DeSantis

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:31.344
is anticipated to announce that he's

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:32.378
running for president.

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.480
South Carolina Senator Tim Scott

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.183
has filed paperwork to do the same.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.951
Former Vice President Mike Pence

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:40.586
likely right behind them.

00:08:40.586 --> 00:08:41.988
Here's something Governor DeSantis

00:08:41.988 --> 00:08:43.890
reportedly told donors on a phone

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:44.490
call this week.

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.258
Quote,

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:46.492
You have basically three people

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:46.926
at this point

00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:48.361
that are credible in this whole thing,

00:08:48.361 --> 00:08:49.996
Biden, Trump and me.

00:08:49.996 --> 00:08:51.464
And I think of those three

00:08:51.464 --> 00:08:53.332
to have a chance to get elected

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.501
Biden and me, unquote.

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:56.302
Do you agree with him

00:08:56.302 --> 00:08:58.404
that Trump cannot win a general election?

00:09:01.107 --> 00:09:02.441
Well well, a couple of things.

00:09:02.441 --> 00:09:03.576
I don't think Trump can win a

00:09:03.576 --> 00:09:04.610
general election,

00:09:04.610 --> 00:09:06.145
but that's a nice way for him to diss

00:09:06.145 --> 00:09:07.113
people like Tim

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:09.348
Scott is a pretty formidable candidate.

00:09:09.348 --> 00:09:09.849
So so

00:09:09.849 --> 00:09:10.850
you just have to take this

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:13.152
as a competitor trying to diss others.

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:13.986
On the other hand,

00:09:13.986 --> 00:09:15.955
they're in the last election cycle,

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:18.224
we saw that in all the swing states,

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.759
almost all

00:09:19.759 --> 00:09:21.260
Georgia, Pennsylvania,

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.429
Nevada and Arizona.

00:09:23.429 --> 00:09:25.164
That trumps that.

00:09:25.164 --> 00:09:26.132
The candidates

00:09:26.132 --> 00:09:28.568
for Senate that Trump endorsed all lost

00:09:29.302 --> 00:09:30.636
If you're taking the votes

00:09:30.636 --> 00:09:32.104
that went to other Republicans

00:09:32.104 --> 00:09:33.306
and put them together,

00:09:33.306 --> 00:09:35.141
those Republicans would have won.

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:36.409
So I think the president's

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:37.577
kind of high profile

00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:39.211
endorsement of those candidates

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:41.447
actually hurt those candidates,

00:09:41.447 --> 00:09:43.149
at least in the general election.

00:09:43.149 --> 00:09:45.217
So if past is Prolog,

00:09:45.217 --> 00:09:45.985
that means President

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:47.320
Trump is going to have a hard time

00:09:47.320 --> 00:09:48.588
in those swing states,

00:09:48.588 --> 00:09:49.755
which means that he cannot win

00:09:49.755 --> 00:09:50.990
a general election.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.525
All right, Senator Bill Cassidy,

00:09:52.525 --> 00:09:53.759
Republican of Louisiana,

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:54.594
good to have you back, sir.

00:09:54.594 --> 00:09:55.227
Thank you so much.

